Here is the complete, production-ready Masked Antarctic Script block to replace your temporary global test.
This code restricts the +100 W/m² longwave perturbation strictly to the Antarctic sea ice pack (South of 50°S). 
It uses the ice_cov(i,j) variable to ensure open ocean grids remain pristine, satisfying your ghost flux requirement.

Step 1: Apply the Final CodeOpen umbase_hg3/src/control/coupling/oasis3_puta2o.F90, locate your T-grid loop, and update it to look exactly like this:
    ! Set up fields from the T grid
    DO j=1,oasis_jmt
      DO i=1,oasis_imt

        ! =================================================================
        ! PRODUCTION: ANTARCTIC SEA ICE GHOST FLUX PERTURBATION
        ! =================================================================
        ! 1. (LAT_P(j) * (180.0 / pi)) converts the grid latitude from radians to degrees.
        ! 2. < -50.0 restricts the forcing to the Southern Ocean / Antarctica.
        ! 3. ice_cov(i,j) > 0.0 ensures it ONLY applies where sea ice is present.
        IF (((LAT_P(j) * (180.0 / pi)) < -50.0) .AND. (ice_cov(i,j) > 0.0)) THEN
            
            ! Apply your targeted downward longwave anomaly (W/m^2)
            c_longwave(i,j) = c_longwave(i,j) + 100.0
            
        ENDIF
        ! =================================================================

        ! Copy various heat flux components
        solar2d(i,j)=c_solar(i,j)
        blue2d(i,j)=c_blue(i,j)
        evap2d(i,j)=c_evap(i,j)
        sublim(i,j)=c_sublim(i,j)
        longwave2d(i,j)=c_longwave(i,j)


